  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.2. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement policies and strategies for creating decent work in the rural economy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The following are some of the major measures to promote decent work in rural areas adopted by local governments and social partners during the biennium, with ILO support:
1) In January 2020, the Government of Sindh promulgated an act to ensure equal rights for women agricultural workers in industrial and other sectors and improve their working conditions
2) Two social dialogue platforms (Provincial Task Force) were established in the agriculture sector (Punjab and Sindh) to promote adherence to fundamental principles and rights at work, focusing especially on lower tiers of the cotton supply chain. A total of 14 collective bargaining agreements were negotiated in this framework.
3) Two new cotton sector farmers&apos; associations were formed in Sindh (in districts Mirpur Khas and Sanghar) in early 2021. 
4) 14 District Vigilance Committees (DVCs) were established to eliminate child and forced labour in rural Districts of Sindh Province.
5) The Bunyad Literacy Community Council improved children&apos;s access to education and established community-based monitoring and remedial mechanisms.  The BLCC developed a Joint Action Plan [JAP] in collaboration and partnership with stakeholders (Literacy Department, Education Department, Health Department, Rescue 1122, Agriculture Department, Department of Labour, Registered Bodies, Trade Unions, relevant communities, and ILO). Under this intervention, the partners established 32 Decent Work Cotton Resource Centres (DCRC) in 8 Union Councils of Tehsil Khairpur Tamianwali; withdrew 1055 working children (5-14 years) from cotton fields; and prevented 245 of their siblings (5-14 years) from entering into child labour. The ILO provided technical assistance for the processes that led to the results, including the provision of relevant and timely information and reports, capacity development of constituents on collective bargaining and child labour, and normative advice on proposed legislation and policy documents, based on relevant international labour standards.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.2.1. Number of member States with measures for decent work in rural areas</narrative>
    </title>
